{
  "description": [
    "System-Level dexterity benchmarks require high-level integration of the hands with robot arms, vision, control, AI,",
    " possibly teleoperation, and more to complete short-horizon 'atomic' tasks.",
    " The short-horizon nature of system-level tasks enables evaluation of the hand dexterous performance without incorporating details like long-horizon multi-step planning.",
    " These atomic tasks were selected to test different",
    " features of dexterity, emphasizing in-hand manipulation."
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Atomic Benchmarking Tasks",
      "description": "Benchmarks covering a broad range of dexterous abilities.",
      "benchmarks": [
        {
          "id": "box-and-blocks",
          "title": "Box and Blocks",
          "primitiveProfile": {
            "manipulation": "Direct",
            "rigidity": "Rigid manipulanda / rigid environment",
            "relativeSize": "Smaller than the hand",
            "controlledDegreesOfFreedom": "Low — one rigid block at a time",
            "constraintComplexity": "Low",
            "constraintChange": "Moderate — repeated grasp, transport, and release",
            "motionRegime": "Quasistatic"
          },
          "shortDescription": "Transfer as many blocks as possible from a cluttered bin to another bin within 60 seconds.",
          "configurationImages": [
            { "src": "Images/task_pictures/box_and_blocks/starting.jpg", "caption": "Starting configuration", "alt": "Blocks arranged in the starting bin" },
            { "src": "Images/task_pictures/box_and_blocks/ending.jpg", "caption": "Ending configuration", "alt": "Blocks transferred into the target bin" }
          ],
          "description": "Starting with blocks in an initial bin, transfer as many blocks as possible over a divider into an adjacent target bin within 60 seconds. This task's setup and procedure are equivalent to Protocol 3a of the YCB Box and Blocks benchmark. Further details on the setup and procedure can be found here.",
          "justification": "Box and Blocks evaluates a system's ability to isolate, grasp, and transport objects from a cluttered environment to a designated target location under time constraints. The task involves quasistatic direct manipulation of rigid blocks in a rigid environment. The blocks are smaller than the hand, and only one block is intentionally controlled at a time, yielding low controlled degrees of freedom and low constraint complexity. High performance still requires reliable grasp acquisition, grasp stability, and efficient object handling, while the repeated grasp, transport, and release cycle produces moderate constraint change. Furthermore, object transport serves as a fundamental building block for many more complex manipulation behaviors, which can often be decomposed into sequences of grasp-and-transport actions.",
          "items": [
            {
              "item": "Bins",
              "quantity": 2,
              "specification": "YCB #69",
              "link": "https://www.ycbbenchmarks.com/object-set/"
            },
            {
              "item": "Lid",
              "quantity": 1,
              "specification": "YCB #70",
              "link": "https://www.ycbbenchmarks.com/object-set/"
            },
            {
              "item": "Blocks",
              "quantity": 100,
              "specification": "YCB #71",
              "link": "https://www.ycbbenchmarks.com/object-set/"
            },
            {
              "item": "Rigid Table",
              "quantity": 1,
              "specification": "Flat rigid work surface capable of holding manipulanda.",
              "link": "https://www.uline.com/Product/Detail/H-6979/Steel-Workbenches/Adjustable-Height-Machine-Table-24-x-18-x-18-25?pricode=WB6636&gadtype=pla&id=H-6979&ad_group_id=150516799157&gad_source=1&gad_campaignid=11612151768&gclid=EAIaIQobChMI2vHI1pKmlQMV_SbUAR01bglwEAQYASABEgLPJvD_BwE"
            }
          ],
          "setup": [
            "Arrange items according to the setup diagram shown in the YCB Box and Blocks protocol.",
            "Randomly distribute the blocks in the initial bin.",
            "The manipulation system's end effector must start outside of both bins."
          ],
          "procedures": [
            "Set up the environment as described above.",
            "During a 60-second period, transfer as many blocks as possible from one bin to the other."
          ],
          "metrics": [
            {
              "name": "Number of Blocks Transferred",
              "unit": "blocks",
              "description": "Number of blocks transferred into the target bin."
            }
          ],
          "executionConstraints": [
            "A transfer is successful only if the block crosses the divider before it is released; blocks may not be tossed over the divider.",
            "Transporting multiple blocks simultaneously counts as one block transferred."
          ],
          "protocolLink": "https://www.ycbbenchmarks.com/protocols-and-benchmarks/"
        },
        {
          "id": "peg-in-hole",
          "title": "Peg-in-Hole",
          "primitiveProfile": {
            "manipulation": "Direct",
            "rigidity": "Rigid manipulanda / rigid environment",
            "relativeSize": "Comparable to the hand",
            "controlledDegreesOfFreedom": "Low — one rigid peg at a time",
            "constraintComplexity": "High — tight position and angle tolerances",
            "constraintChange": "High — free motion to constrained insertion",
            "motionRegime": "Quasistatic"
          },
          "shortDescription": "Insert pegs into a pegboard with holes of various shapes and tolerances.",
          "configurationImages": [
            { "src": "Images/task_pictures/peg_in_hole/starting.jpg", "caption": "Starting configuration", "alt": "NIST assembly task board before assembly" },
            { "src": "Images/task_pictures/peg_in_hole/ending.jpg", "caption": "Ending configuration", "alt": "NIST assembly task board after assembly" }
          ],
          "description": "Insert pegs into the NIST Assembly Task Board M1 with holes of various shapes and tolerances. This task's setup and procedure are equivalent to a single round of ManipulationNet's peg insertion task. Further details on the setup and procedure can be found here.",
          "justification": "Peg-in-Hole evaluates a system's ability to perform precision assembly under tight geometric tolerances. The task involves quasistatic direct manipulation of one rigid peg at a time within a rigid fixture and environment. Each peg is comparable in size to the hand, and controlling a single rigid peg produces low controlled degrees of freedom. The task nevertheless exhibits high constraint complexity because successful completion requires satisfying multiple geometric constraints simultaneously within narrow positional and angular tolerances. It also features high constraint change as the interaction progresses from unconstrained free-space motion to increasingly restrictive contact conditions during insertion. More broadly, peg insertion serves as a canonical example of contact-rich assembly and is representative of a wide range of industrial manufacturing operations.",
          "items": [
            {
              "item": "NIST Assembly Task Board M1",
              "quantity": 1,
              "specification": "NIST Assembly Task Board M1",
              "link": "https://manipulation-net.org/tasks/peg_in_hole.html"
            },
            {
              "item": "Pegs",
              "quantity": 5,
              "specification": "Corresponding circle, hexagon, triangle, rectangle and L-shape pegs",
              "link": "https://manipulation-net.org/tasks/peg_in_hole.html"
            },
            {
              "item": "Peg Holder",
              "quantity": 1,
              "specification": "Corresponding Peg-holder",
              "link": "https://manipulation-net.org/tasks/peg_in_hole.html"
            },
            {
              "item": "Rigid Table",
              "quantity": 1,
              "specification": "Flat rigid work surface capable of holding manipulanda.",
              "link": "https://www.uline.com/Product/Detail/H-6979/Steel-Workbenches/Adjustable-Height-Machine-Table-24-x-18-x-18-25?pricode=WB6636&gadtype=pla&id=H-6979&ad_group_id=150516799157&gad_source=1&gad_campaignid=11612151768&gclid=EAIaIQobChMI2vHI1pKmlQMV_SbUAR01bglwEAQYASABEgLPJvD_BwE"
            }
          ],
          "setup": [
            "Place both the assembly task board and peg holder on the table in any preferred configuration."
          ],
          "procedures": [
            "Place the pegs and pegboard in the prescribed starting positions, then select a pegboard row, numbered 1 through 4, to fill.",
            "Grasp the peg whose shape corresponds to the target hole.",
            "Align and insert the peg into the target hole.",
            "Repeat for all five peg-hole pairs. The insertion order is A(n), B(n), C(n), D(n), E(n)."
          ],
          "metrics": [
            {
              "name": "Pegs Inserted",
              "unit": "pegs",
              "description": "Number of pegs successfully inserted."
            }
          ],
          "executionConstraints": [
            "Any manipulation strategy may be used.",
            "The task must be completed within three hours."
          ],
          "protocolLink": "https://manipulation-net.org/tasks/peg_in_hole.html"
        },
        {
          "id": "pick-up-flat-object",
          "title": "Pick Up Flat Object",
          "primitiveProfile": {
            "manipulation": "Direct",
            "rigidity": "Rigid manipulanda / rigid environment",
            "relativeSize": "Smaller than the hand",
            "controlledDegreesOfFreedom": "Low — one rigid object",
            "constraintComplexity": "High — support severely restricts grasp contacts and approaches",
            "constraintChange": "Moderate — table contact to hand support",
            "motionRegime": "Quasistatic"
          },
          "shortDescription": "Stably grasp an M6 washer initially lying flat on a rigid table.",
          "configurationImages": [
            { "src": "Images/task_pictures/grasp_flat_object/starting.jpg", "caption": "Starting configuration", "alt": "Washer lying flat on the table" },
            { "src": "Images/task_pictures/grasp_flat_object/ending.jpg", "caption": "Ending configuration", "alt": "Washer lifted above the table" }
          ],
          "description": "Grasp and lift an M6 washer initially resting flat on a rigid tabletop to a specified height without dropping it.",
          "justification": "Pick Up Flat Object evaluates a system's ability to acquire and maintain a stable grasp on a thin object resting on a supporting surface. The task involves quasistatic direct manipulation of one rigid object that is smaller than the hand within a rigid environment, producing low controlled degrees of freedom. Unlike conventional object-relocation tasks, the rigid supporting surface severely restricts access to the object, creating high constraint complexity by sharply limiting feasible contact locations and grasp approaches. Successful completion also requires managing the transition from table contact to hand support, producing moderate constraint change during grasp acquisition. More broadly, grasping thin objects is representative of many real-world manipulation scenarios involving washers, coins, cards, sheets, and other low-profile objects that are challenging to isolate from supporting surfaces.",
          "items": [
            {
              "item": "M6 washer",
              "quantity": 1,
              "specification": "Stainless Steel M6 Washer.",
              "link": "https://www.mcmaster.com/91701A621/"
            },
            {
              "item": "Rigid Table",
              "quantity": 1,
              "specification": "Flat rigid work surface capable of holding manipulanda.",
              "link": "https://www.uline.com/Product/Detail/H-6979/Steel-Workbenches/Adjustable-Height-Machine-Table-24-x-18-x-18-25?pricode=WB6636&gadtype=pla&id=H-6979&ad_group_id=150516799157&gad_source=1&gad_campaignid=11612151768&gclid=EAIaIQobChMI2vHI1pKmlQMV_SbUAR01bglwEAQYASABEgLPJvD_BwE"
            }
          ],
          "setup": [
            "Place the washer flat on the tabletop near the center of the table.",
            "The manipulator shall begin each trial with the nearest point on the end effector at least 100 mm away from the washer."
          ],
          "procedures": [
            "Position the manipulator in the prescribed starting configuration.",
            "Transport the washer to a height of at least 2 cm above the tabletop.",
            "Maintain control of the washer for a minimum of 3 seconds while keeping it stationary and above the required height.",
            "A trial is successful if the washer is lifted to the required height and remains stationary within the target region for the allotted time."
          ],
          "metrics": [
            {
              "name": "Total Task Completion Time",
              "unit": "seconds",
              "description": "Time required to complete the task."
            }
          ],
          "executionConstraints": [
            "Any method may be used to grasp, lift, and hold the washer at the required height.",
            "The task must be completed within 60 seconds."
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "tie-a-knot",
          "title": "Tie a Knot",
          "primitiveProfile": {
            "manipulation": "Direct",
            "rigidity": "Deformable manipulanda / rigid environment",
            "relativeSize": "Mixed relative to the hand",
            "controlledDegreesOfFreedom": "High — continuously deformable rope",
            "constraintComplexity": "High — contact and topological constraints",
            "constraintChange": "High — evolving contacts and topology",
            "motionRegime": "Quasistatic"
          },
          "shortDescription": "Tie a rope into a tight overhand knot.",
          "configurationImages": [
            { "src": "Images/task_pictures/tie_a_knot/starting.jpg", "caption": "Starting configuration", "alt": "Untied rope on the table" },
            { "src": "Images/task_pictures/tie_a_knot/ending.jpg", "caption": "Ending configuration", "alt": "Rope tied in an overhand knot" }
          ],
          "description": "Tie a rope into a tight overhand knot.",
          "justification": "Tie a Knot evaluates a system's ability to manipulate a deformable object whose geometry changes continuously throughout the task. The task involves quasistatic direct manipulation of a deformable rope in a rigid environment. Its diameter is smaller than the hand while its length is larger, giving it mixed relative size, and its continuously changing shape produces high controlled degrees of freedom. Successful completion requires coordinating intermediate configurations while controlling the rope's global shape, local contacts, and self-contacts. Knot formation also imposes topological constraints, producing high constraint complexity and high constraint change as contacts and topology evolve. More broadly, knot tying serves as a representative benchmark for deformable-object manipulation and captures many of the challenges encountered when handling ropes, cables, sutures, and other flexible materials.",
          "items": [
            {
              "item": "rope",
              "quantity": 1,
              "specification": "50 cm long 1/4 in diameter low stretch polyester plastic rope.",
              "link": "https://www.mcmaster.com/3132T131/"
            },
            {
              "item": "Rigid Table",
              "quantity": 1,
              "specification": "Flat rigid work surface capable of holding manipulanda.",
              "link": "https://www.uline.com/Product/Detail/H-6979/Steel-Workbenches/Adjustable-Height-Machine-Table-24-x-18-x-18-25?pricode=WB6636&gadtype=pla&id=H-6979&ad_group_id=150516799157&gad_source=1&gad_campaignid=11612151768&gclid=EAIaIQobChMI2vHI1pKmlQMV_SbUAR01bglwEAQYASABEgLPJvD_BwE"
            }
          ],
          "setup": [
            "Place the rope near the center of the table in any configuration that does not self-intersect.",
            "The manipulator shall begin each trial with the nearest point on the end effector at least 100 mm away from all of the manipulanda."
          ],
          "procedures": [
            "Position the manipulator in the prescribed starting configuration.",
            "Manipulate the rope to tie an overhand knot.",
            "Release the tied rope onto the table.",
            "A trial is successful if a valid overhand knot remains intact after release with no visible slack in the knot."
          ],
          "metrics": [
            {
              "name": "Total Task Completion Time",
              "unit": "seconds",
              "description": "Time required to complete the task."
            }
          ],
          "executionConstraints": [
            "Any manipulation strategy may be used.",
            "The task must be completed within 60 seconds."
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "twist-lid-on-jar",
          "title": "Twist Lid on Jar",
          "primitiveProfile": {
            "manipulation": "Direct",
            "rigidity": "Rigid manipulanda / rigid environment",
            "relativeSize": "Comparable to the hand",
            "controlledDegreesOfFreedom": "Low — one movable rigid lid",
            "constraintComplexity": "High — threaded alignment and torque",
            "constraintChange": "High — free motion to thread engagement",
            "motionRegime": "Quasistatic"
          },
          "shortDescription": "Pick up a regular mouth round jar lid from a table and thread and tighten it onto a fixed jar.",
          "configurationImages": [
            { "src": "Images/task_pictures/twist_lid/starting.jpg", "caption": "Starting configuration", "alt": "Jar and detached lid in their starting positions" },
            { "src": "Images/task_pictures/twist_lid/ending.jpg", "caption": "Ending configuration", "alt": "Lid threaded onto the jar" }
          ],
          "description": "Pick up a regular mouth round jar lid from a table and thread and tighten it onto a fixed jar.",
          "justification": "Twist a Lid on Jar evaluates a system's ability to perform contact-rich assembly involving both translational and rotational manipulation. The task involves quasistatic direct manipulation of one movable rigid lid, comparable in size to the hand, against a rigid jar and environment. Controlling a single movable rigid body produces low controlled degrees of freedom. The task nevertheless exhibits high constraint complexity because successful completion depends on satisfying the threaded interface geometry while maintaining a stable grasp and applying sufficient torque. It also involves high constraint change as the interaction progresses from free-space motion to initial contact, thread engagement, and fully constrained rotational tightening. More broadly, lid threading is representative of household and industrial assembly operations that require alignment, insertion, and controlled rotational force.",
          "items": [
            {
              "item": "jar lid",
              "quantity": 1,
              "specification": "89-400 regular-mouth round plastic jar lid",
              "link": "https://www.uline.com/Product/Detail/S-9936/Jars/Clear-Round-Wide-Mouth-Plastic-Jars-16-oz-White-Cap?pricode=WB0644&gadtype=pla&id=S-9936&ad_group_id=152179486982&gad_source=1&gad_campaignid=11612151543&gclid=Cj0KCQjwguLSBhDLARIsAH-yPrELFzXivNndELEB9E2T3k6Yjjk5g-u3pHuzmfw575vte0hAn15mJ2IaArQNEALw_wcB"
            },
            {
              "item": "Regular-mouth jar",
              "quantity": 1,
              "specification": "Any plastic jar that is compatible with the lid",
              "link": "https://www.uline.com/Product/Detail/S-9936/Jars/Clear-Round-Wide-Mouth-Plastic-Jars-16-oz-White-Cap?pricode=WB0644&gadtype=pla&id=S-9936&ad_group_id=152179486982&gad_source=1&gad_campaignid=11612151543&gclid=Cj0KCQjwguLSBhDLARIsAH-yPrELFzXivNndELEB9E2T3k6Yjjk5g-u3pHuzmfw575vte0hAn15mJ2IaArQNEALw_wcB"
            },
            {
              "item": "Rigid mounting fixture",
              "quantity": 1,
