          ],
          "description": "Button a button on a buttoning board.",
          "justification": "Fasten Button evaluates a system's ability to perform precision manipulation under tight geometric constraints involving mixed rigid and deformable manipulanda in a rigid environment. The task requires quasistatic direct manipulation of a rigid button that is smaller than the hand while interacting with deformable fabric. Coordinating the button pose with localized fabric deformation produces moderate controlled degrees of freedom. The task exhibits high constraint complexity because successful completion depends on satisfying multiple geometric constraints while regulating fingertip forces and maintaining stable contact. It also involves high constraint change, progressing from free-space manipulation to buttonhole contact, partial insertion, and complete passage through the fabric. More broadly, button fastening represents fine manipulation tasks encountered in dressing, garment handling, and interaction with small everyday objects.",
